        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioner (Bryan Stevenson), joe Sullivan was 13 years of age when he was arrested with two older boys, convicted of sexual assault, and sentenced to life without parole."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioner (Bryan Stevenson)",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "dd9ec30a59879ca7c13408819db5dee18608b0e19b294cd9c4782afe55493bf7",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-dd9ec30a5987-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "He is one of only two children this age who have ever been sentenced to life without parole for a non\u2011homicide offense, and no child has received such a sentence for non\u2011homicide in the past 18 years."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Stevenson",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "dd9ec30a59879ca7c13408819db5dee18608b0e19b294cd9c4782afe55493bf7",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-dd9ec30a5987-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 21,
              "start": 21
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Stevenson, petitioner asks the Court to adopt a rule that bans life without parole for any child under the age of 14."
      }
    ],
